    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=4$, $b=4$. Eight families own cars; their 12 cars include four cars beyond one per family.",
      "worked": "The two zero-car families leave $10-2=8$ families who own cars.\n\nThe total number of cars is $10\\times1.2=12$. Giving each of these eight families one car accounts for eight cars. The extra $12-8=4$ cars mean that four families own two cars.\n\n$b=4$ and $a=8-4=4$.\n\nCheck: $2+4+4=10$ families and $(0\\times2+1\\times4+2\\times4)\\div10=1.2$ cars.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
